  "hunk_reviews": [
    {
      "hunk": 1,
      "file": "src/cdk/collections/selection-model.ts",
      "header": "@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ export class SelectionModel<T> {",
      "judgment": "setSelection canonicalizes each prospective value against the existing concrete selection before the deletion phase. A distinct real option with the same public value must retain the already-selected option identity. Both minimum complete algorithms also canonicalize the removed-value predicate; reverting only the new Set expression is therefore insufficient to reproduce the old defect. The complete-original-algorithm reversion is rejected. Own no model implementation or private helper."
    },
    {
      "hunk": 2,
      "file": "src/cdk/collections/selection.spec.ts",
      "header": "@@ -300,6 +300,17 @@ describe('SelectionModel', () => {",
      "judgment": "The added upstream regression invokes the public single-selection model twice with distinct comparator-equivalent values and disabled notifications. The earlier whole-authenticated-module diagnostic executes that original condition. The unchanged packed two-call assertion and the new eight-phase genuine-list probe additionally require public identity, getters, real nodes/ARIA and exact event histories. The second list supplies valid option instances, and every state requires its own model/getters/nodes to remain untouched. These requirements do not imply that a source protocol or synthetic admission control is a packed/native/floor pass."
    }
  ],
  "source_conclusion": "Inherit the complete public SelectionModel comparator fix through the advertised current CDK peer. Both exact minimum public collections closures implement concrete-value canonicalization and retain a real selected option when setSelection receives a distinct comparator-equivalent option. Four owned constructors in three files use identity-only models and no owned caller invokes setSelection; the public selection-list model nevertheless permits application comparator and selection changes. Preserve that public capability without a CDK fork, private import, consumer API migration or component/style change. The original two-call regression remains independently required. The added packed probe must use actual options from two real legacy lists, retain the first list model/options/nodes, observe exact selected identities/getters/ARIA and all reentrant event payloads across eight phases, leave the second list untouched and unsubscribe its own observer. Exact untouched tagged receiver methods with complete authentic peer models explain the historical duplicate emissions; explicit callback/HTML protocols are source diagnostics only. Require the original assertion, equal raw/selected rich observation, full106 current-clean same-run packed evidence and exact artifact identity before runtime admission. Compiler, Node/RxJS, native and remaining peer floors, all authored uses and complete G11 remain separately pending.",
  "decision": "Inherit the complete public SelectionModel comparator fix through the advertised current CDK peer. Both exact minimum public collections closures implement concrete-value canonicalization and retain a real selected option when setSelection receives a distinct comparator-equivalent option. Four owned constructors in three files use identity-only models and no owned caller invokes setSelection; the public selection-list model nevertheless permits application comparator and selection changes. Preserve that public capability without a CDK fork, private import, consumer API migration or component/style change. The original two-call regression remains independently required. The added packed probe must use actual options from two real legacy lists, retain the first list model/options/nodes, observe exact selected identities/getters/ARIA and all reentrant event payloads across eight phases, leave the second list untouched and unsubscribe its own observer. Exact untouched tagged receiver methods with complete authentic peer models explain the historical duplicate emissions; explicit callback/HTML protocols are source diagnostics only. Require the original assertion, equal raw/selected rich observation, full106 current-clean same-run packed evidence and exact artifact identity before runtime admission. Compiler, Node/RxJS, native and remaining peer floors, all authored uses and complete G11 remain separately pending.",
